 "result": "csvsum.py is a streaming dict-based summer. It reads stdin as bytes, splits on newlines and commas, converts each val to integer cents with round(float*100), and writes sorted 'cat,sum' lines with 2 decimals and a sign. It matches the public sample out-0 exactly and runs in about 0.39 s on 1M rows. It is registered as baseline 1.91398 (noise 1.5%). Two variants (pre-split rows; try/except accumulation) did not beat it by more than 3%, so I'm stopping here and returning the unspent energy to the lineage store.",
